# What the tests read. Copy this file to `.env.test`, which git ignores, and fill in the services
# you want them to meet for real. A service left as it is keeps its fake.
#
# Bun loads this file into every `bun test`, so it holds the default for every run, and one run can
# say otherwise without the file being touched:
#
#   HCLOUD_MODE=real bun test tests/convex/allocations   meets Hetzner, for that run
#   HCLOUD_MODE=fake bun test                            keeps the fake, whatever the file says
#
# See `docs/setups/hetzner-cloud.md`. The project a run meets must hold nothing else: it makes its
# own firewall, labels everything it creates, removes all of it at the end, and removes what a
# killed run left behind, so anything still in that project afterwards is a leak.
HCLOUD_MODE=fake
HCLOUD_TOKEN=
